  "title": "# Build: home-cards-live (Urgent profile) - replaces pending item `home-cards` Brett, Nov 3 2026 (v…",
  "asked": "# Build: home-cards-live (Urgent profile) - replaces pending item `home-cards` Brett, Nov 3 2026 (voice): \"I shouldn't need to build cards. I should draw dynamic data.\" Assigned agent: **Ping Paulie** (book on his card; if busy and the all-rounder router is on main, whoever is free - record who). Register in Urgent (id `home-cards-live`) + banner entry. Mark pending item `home-cards` replaced by this build (pending_change status, note) - do NOT hand-build a card per plugin. ## What to build: one card engine that draws any data - s1 `card@1` asset = a data binding, not a design: {source: any control@1 / plugin-commands-auto read command (REST/MCP/CLI already generated for every plugin), args, path into the result, view: number | list | meter | chart (line/bar/spark) | feed | table | status, refresh: live (subscribe to the live feed when the source has one) or every N s, title, icon, size}. Open registry for views. Tokens/assets only. - s2 **Add card** on Home: pick any plugin -> any of its read commands -> preview the live result -> pick a view (smart default from the data shape: single number -> number, array -> list/table, time series -> chart, status field -> status) -> pick fields -> Save. Zero code, zero agents, zero tokens. - s3 **Drag any hook / data element onto Home** (use the `hook@1` / `drop-target@1` contract from the toolbar build if on main, else define Home as a drop target the same way and note it) -> configure dialog prefilled -> card. - s4 Home layout: drag to reorder, resize, show/hide, card context menu (Edit card, Change view, Size, Open plugin, Remove), Show all / Hide all, saved per user on axHub. The 5 existing Home cards become card@1 assets bound to their existing data. - s5 Starter set auto-offered (not hand-built): one-tap 'Suggested cards' from whatever read commands exist (builds running, today's cost, agents working, approvals waiting, UI Review waiting, notes recent). - s6 Zero-token test (no LLM imports in the card engine), tests for binding/live refresh/view picking, phone + desktop screenshots, UI Review item, report `_claude/builds/reports/home-cards-live.md`, THREADS, PR, steps through the store. Commits clean and professional. Watch live: Brett can watch the screen you are changing hot-render in the console. Whenever you start work on a screen or element, run `node framework/cli/axf.mjs focus <app> [route] [css-selector] --note \"<what you are changing>\"` (apps: console-web, axhub-web, amberx-droid, walkthrough-studio, demo, framework, console, axhub-android, voicevault). Agent cap: heavy steps (pnpm/npm/vite builds, docker node:22 test runs, Playwright) share a VPS-wide lock. Run each one as `node /opt/axf/deploy/../framework/cli/agent-slots.mjs heavy -- <command>` so only a few run at once. Model switches (Brett, Nov 3 2026): a downgrade (e.g. Fable → Opus) is fine. An UPGRADE (e.g. Opus → Fable) needs Brett's approval: when you reach one, run `node apps/console-web/plugins/build-orchestrator/orchestrator.mjs request-upgrade <id> <phase>`, ask once, and stop. Never approve a model switch upgrade yourself (no `act approve` on an upgrade), never relaunch on a higher model.",
